    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3769b5ca3fe55f95ac29f83bad0ece5bb78b82f612328617690e808d72d6dce0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source's equivalent and sufficient criteria relocate RH into different failure interfaces: an oversized prime-counting error, a nonreal zero before the heat-flow transition, a violated divisor inequality, or excessive Möbius partial-sum growth. The false sharp Mertens bound and eventual sign changes of π-Li then show why long finite agreement with any such global pattern does not settle the universally quantified criterion.",
