    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8dab21ffc10ad02334b664693a2e73d0f5fd54334cd8b134a0685f28e021b86f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The physical encodings in the source have three different logical strengths. Logarithmic energies and unique factorization construct a partition-function representation of ζ in its defining series regime; the spin-system route then shows that a formula involving ζ is insufficient when the available circle theorem does not cover the actual interaction; and the billiard route is reported with a separate RH-equivalent nested asymptotic criterion. A useful translation must therefore preserve the hypotheses or equivalence needed for the intended conclusion, not merely reproduce ζ symbolically.",
