    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a8147e1e356b8991a358c783e652aaff5ac6f848fb848d245c2f7467e6daf1d0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses GUE at two distinct scales: unfolded eigenvalue statistics model local repulsion among zero ordinates, while characteristic-polynomial moments provide a universal factor for conjectural zeta moments only after a separate Euler product restores prime-specific arithmetic. Together the sections show that random-matrix universality is predictive across zeros and values, but is not an arithmetic-complete or RH-validating model by itself.",
