      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ff49434662879dbdb96059553c1b4497571071db6b375e29e51ed9003006a0bf",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the source, reproducing spectral data ranges from matching only a leading counting law, to realizing a preselected sequence, to explicitly transforming an equally spaced oscillator spectrum into the trivial zeros. These constructions show progressively stronger forms of spectral reproduction, yet none supplies the exhaustive, self-adjoint, chaotic mechanism required by the proposed nontrivial-zero program.",
